meta {
  name: Update Profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/me
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Bruno Tester",
    "bio": "Checking in from the terminal.",
    "hometown": "Truckee, CA"
  }
}

docs {
  Partial update — send only the fields you want to change. Expect 200 with
  the full updated profile.

  Passing null clears a field: {"bio": null} removes the bio, and
  {"avatarKey": null} removes the photo. Omitting a field leaves it alone,
  which is a different thing from sending null. hometown is the exception:
  it is required, so it can be changed but not cleared.

  iOS sends name, bio, hometown and avatarKey together in one request after an avatar
  upload, so a profile edit is a single write with one place for errors.
}
